    "updated_at": "2025-05-29T23:54:50Z",
    "body": "Seems like the same problem exists for the `accessor` context. Here’s a way we’ve been hitting it in Ladybird:\n\n```html\n<div id=foo></div>\n<script>\n    const request = window.indexedDB.open(\"foo\", 4);\n    window.location.reload();\n    request.addEventListener(\"success\", function(e) {\n        console.log(\"success\", window.foo.nodeName);\n    });\n</script>\n```",
