    "created_at": "2025-06-05T14:51:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-05T14:51:20Z",
    "body": "I guess for the first example you could add an assert in step 2 of the [check if an access between two browsing contexts should be reported](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#coop-check-access-report).\n\nThat said, in [destroy a child navigable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#destroy-a-child-navigable) you are destroying the 'content navigable' for the iframe. Which means that you get a null [content window ](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#content-window). So when you are doing:\n\n1. Let W be the value of the [[[Window]]](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-windowproxy-window) internal slot of this.\n\n1. [Check if an access between two browsing contexts should be reported](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#coop-check-access-report), given the [current global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#current-global-object)'s [browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#window-bc), W's [browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#window-bc), P, and the [current settings object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#current-settings-object).\n\nI think step 1 would fail because you are trying to get the internal slot of a null value no? This is called on the WindowProxy, which should be null since the iframe was removed.\n\nI don't see how you get in the situation with the accessor context being null from your second example. Could you precise which of the three different calls to window has the issue?",
